--TEST--
An `@example` outside every directory the test corpus walks is `E0325`, asked before the file is looked for at all — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-see-and-example`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The directory question is asked first and answers on the written path
// alone, so a path outside every walked directory is refused for being there
// rather than for a file that would not have helped it. This one names no
// file either, and the code says which of the two answered.
/// A till, documented with an example nothing compiles.
///
/// @example src/charge.nvs
final class Till {
    public static function charge(): int {
        return 0;
    }
}
echo Till::charge(), "\n";
